{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition","id":1526737,"title":"Things to like W5 for or why so many people hate new edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-13T03:51:11-08:00","id":1526737,"title":"Things to like W5 for or why so many people hate new edition?","content":"Well, after reading of W5 corebook, I can say... surprisengly, I like it. Didn't try the system, but lore is huge improvement for Garou. New edition in fact, retcon the bigger part of their crimes.<br /> Namely:<br /> 1) No more kinfolk, hense no more eugenic, sex slavery or bestiality in case of Lupus.<br /> 2) Impergium is something that happened so long ago that Garou themselves barely know what did actully happenthan. The 'Delirium-as-collective-human-mental-trauma' is just a theory.<br /> 3) War of Rage? Wtf is this? Considering, that other Fera are pretty much aliens who Garou barely know anything about.<br /> 4) No more Crinos-borned and descrimination toward them<br /> 5) Since Garou have no history anymore, just an oral tradition, there isn't invasion in Americas, War of Tears, Swords of Heimdal and other 'great deeds' Garou were so famous for. Well, at least for now. Not guilty until proven guilty, etc.<br /> 6) Finally, Vampires are not 'Wyrmlings' by default. Like, leeches are still cruel, lying and sneaky bastards... but that stereotype about vampires gonna support like almost any denizen of WoD. First and foremost, vampires themselves.<br /> <br /> TL/DR, authors retconed most of controversies that taunted WtA in past editions. I can't find any objective reason for haters to bush Garou. Now they are... eccentialy, they are pretty close to status of the &quot;good guys&quot;.<br /> \u200bwhat's wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T06:37:49-08:00","id":1526742,"title":"","content":"There's a thread called &quot;<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5\">Review of W5</a>&quot; that goes over the book in great detail and discussions of the issues people have with it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> Also, I'd recommend to you <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/werewolf-5th-and-86463964\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a> from James F. Sambrano who worked on the Hunters Entertainment version of W5. That is necessary context for some of the anger this game generated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T07:03:26-08:00","id":1526746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition#post1526737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) No more kinfolk, hense no more eugenic, sex slavery or bestiality in case of Lupus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you think new lupus come from, given W5 does hint it MIGHT be a bloodline thing? Just because kinfolk are gone, does not mean there isn't sex between garou and wolves.<br /> <br /> I really wish this goddamn argument didn't keep popping up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition#post1526737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) Since Garou have no history anymore, just an oral tradition, there isn't invasion in Americas, War of Tears, Swords of Heimdal and other 'great deeds' Garou were so famous for. Well, at least for now. Not guilty until proven guilty, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of those things happened, just that there wasn't a (known) garou-specific event.<br /> <br /> Also, the last two aren't even celebrated by the garou in Legacy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T07:56:07-08:00","id":1526752,"title":"","content":"It's a half-baked facsimile of an edition made by people who were barely qualified to tinker with Vampire, and who neither understand W:tA's problems nor have any willingness to actually address them. They fucked this up, they fucked up H:tR, and they're going to fuck up everything else because they think that everything should look, play, and feel like V:tM.<br /> <br /> Oh, their particular interpretation of V:tM. If you don't want that, your fun is wrong and bad and you should feel bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T08:04:57-08:00","id":1526754,"title":"","content":"Yes, Lashet. We do know you don't know what old Werewolf was about.<br /> <br /> But do tell me, is there anything you like about this game without comparing it to your vision of what old Werewolf was? Are there any games you want to play? Is there anything that makes you want to make a campaign and run it for a dozen sessions for someone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T08:22:45-08:00","id":1526757,"title":"","content":"I don't have a lot of skin in the W5-drama. Werewolf interests me, but it's not one of my top favourite game-lines. I've also already resigned myself to sticking with X20 for the most part.<br /> <br /> But, reading your list, I can't help but wonder if you realize that most of the things you see as Upsides of the new edition are precisely the sorts of things that most of the older fans are Upset about?<br /> <br /> I'm not going to say that WtA didn't have some issues, and could have used some rehashing to deal with some of the worst examples. But, broadly speaking, the fact that the Garou are tragic assholes with millennia of catastrophic screw-ups and monstrous traditions is a Feature, not a Bug, for a lot of Werewolf fans. And your list of examples mostly seems to be &quot;hey look, they took the Darkness out of the World of Darkness, isn't that great?&quot; Taking all of the ugliness and moral-Grey out of the Garou turns their struggle into a truly Black-and-White one. And while Werewolf has always been closer to that than most of the other WoD gamelines, it's still supposed to have grit and nuance.<br /> <br /> Just trying to surgically remove all of that stuff entirely to avoid dealing with the complications probably strikes a lot of people as a lazy method of confronting the actual issues that even fans are willing to acknowledge. The Controversies weren't an accident. They were The Point. And a lot of people don't like the alternative that they've been offered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T08:58:05-08:00","id":1526761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition#post1526737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, after reading of W5 corebook, I can say... surprisengly, I like it. Didn't try the system, but lore is huge improvement for Garou. New edition in fact, retcon the bigger part of their crimes.<br /> Namely:<br /> 1) No more kinfolk, hense no more eugenic, sex slavery or bestiality in case of Lupus.<br /> 2) Impergium is something that happened so long ago that Garou themselves barely know what did actully happenthan. The 'Delirium-as-collective-human-mental-trauma' is just a theory.<br /> 3) War of Rage? Wtf is this? Considering, that other Fera are pretty much aliens who Garou barely know anything about.<br /> 4) No more Crinos-borned and descrimination toward them<br /> 5) Since Garou have no history anymore, just an oral tradition, there isn't invasion in Americas, War of Tears, Swords of Heimdal and other 'great deeds' Garou were so famous for. Well, at least for now. Not guilty until proven guilty, etc.<br /> 6) Finally, Vampires are not 'Wyrmlings' by default. Like, leeches are still cruel, lying and sneaky bastards... but that stereotype about vampires gonna support like almost any denizen of WoD. First and foremost, vampires themselves.<br /> <br /> TL/DR, authors retconed most of controversies that taunted WtA in past editions. I can't find any objective reason for haters to bush Garou. Now they are... eccentialy, they are pretty close to status of the &quot;good guys&quot;.<br /> \u200bwhat's wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wanted to make sure, I got this right... So to add to my first post:<br /> <br /> I think one issue is that you should re-read the book because most of your points don't accurately describe W5:<br /> <br /> 1) Bloodlines still matter to Garou. And Silver Fangs still consider themselves to be a &quot;hereditary aristocracy&quot;, for example. The only difference is that the ugly stuff isn't directly mentioned. But this book hasn't gone so far as to make it impossible.<br /> 2) The Impergium happened in W5. That's one of the key-pillars of Garou-lore that still remains in W5. And Delirium as a result of that is a fact, not a theory. What you're referring to is probably that one in-character letter which is merely speculating on how it maybe works.<br /> 3) The War of Rage happened in W5. From pg 284: &quot;The Garou wish they knew, for it might make interacting with these other shapechangers less volatile. Sometimes, other shifters indicate that some long-ago grudge shaped the relationship the Garou have with them today \u2014 which would certainly be in keeping with today\u2019s Garou bearing the responsibility of past times of legend.\u200b&quot; The only weird part is that the Garou have somehow completely forgotten that this has happened.<br /> 4) Well, at least we got the W5 corebook shitting on wolf-born Garou now instead...<br /> 5) &quot;Since Garou have no history anymore, just an oral tradition&quot; certainly describes the approach but also is a stupid idea. It's an ahistoric notion that one would only arrive at due to poor research or knowledge. Oral history is a thing that works. Oral tradition isn't an explanation for erasing history. But also:<ul><li>Invasion of America: Still happened. From pg 39 &quot;Modern Garou scholars hang their heads in shame as they recall such events as the slaughter of Garou and Kin in North America\u200b&quot;</li> <li>War of Tears: Not the Bunyip but still happened. From the same page: &quot;and the subjugation of the Philippine Luntiang Kuko, a sept of witch-wolves that had protected the archipelago and significant portions of Southeast Asia.\u200b&quot;</li> <li>Swords of Heimdall: Well, now all the Fenrir are fascists, so if anything W5 is doubling down on the fascism-angle from previous editions. Now you have even more Sword of Heimdall than before in your WtA-game!</li> </ul>6) Okay... what you're describing isn't really a change. Before vampires were enemies because of what they did and their association with the Wyrm. Now they're enemies because of what they do, they're still the same antagonists they were in previous editions. It's not like the book listed some kind of &quot;Here's the vampire who works together with the Garou!&quot;-NPC in the book. I know the previews made some claims about changing the status of vampires in relation to Garou but the book we've got hasn't gone through with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T10:44:27-08:00","id":1526767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526754#post1526754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Lashet. We do know you don't know what old Werewolf was about.<br /> <br /> But do tell me, is there anything you like about this game without comparing it to your vision of what old Werewolf was? Are there any games you want to play? Is there anything that makes you want to make a campaign and run it for a dozen sessions for someone?</div> </div> </div> </div>That still an urban-fantasy game with werewolves, who can be pretty badass compare to vampires. IIRC, no Mithra, Yaga, Seth and other werewolf-stomping vampires in canon right now. Not even disciplines beynd 5 dots. Hense, not that much of humilation. And now Garou are barely have a reason to be hated by fandom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T11:16:41-08:00","id":1526768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526761#post1526761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wanted to make sure, I got this right... So to add to my first post:<br /> <br /> I think one issue is that you should re-read the book because most of your points don't accurately describe W5:<br /> <br /> 1) Bloodlines still matter to Garou. And Silver Fangs still consider themselves to be a &quot;hereditary aristocracy&quot;, for example. The only difference is that the ugly stuff isn't directly mentioned. But this book hasn't gone so far as to make it impossible.<br /> 2) The Impergium happened in W5. That's one of the key-pillars of Garou-lore that still remains in W5. And Delirium as a result of that is a fact, not a theory. What you're referring to is probably that one in-character letter which is merely speculating on how it maybe works.<br /> 3) The War of Rage happened in W5. From pg 284: &quot;The Garou wish they knew, for it might make interacting with these other shapechangers less volatile. Sometimes, other shifters indicate that some long-ago grudge shaped the relationship the Garou have with them today \u2014 which would certainly be in keeping with today\u2019s Garou bearing the responsibility of past times of legend.\u200b&quot; The only weird part is that the Garou have somehow completely forgotten that this has happened.<br /> 4) Well, at least we got the W5 corebook shitting on wolf-born Garou now instead...<br /> 5) &quot;Since Garou have no history anymore, just an oral tradition&quot; certainly describes the approach but also is a stupid idea. It's an ahistoric notion that one would only arrive at due to poor research or knowledge. Oral history is a thing that works. Oral tradition isn't an explanation for erasing history. But also:<ul><li>Invasion of America: Still happened. From pg 39 &quot;Modern Garou scholars hang their heads in shame as they recall such events as the slaughter of Garou and Kin in North America\u200b&quot;</li> <li>War of Tears: Not the Bunyip but still happened. From the same page: &quot;and the subjugation of the Philippine Luntiang Kuko, a sept of witch-wolves that had protected the archipelago and significant portions of Southeast Asia.\u200b&quot;</li> <li>Swords of Heimdall: Well, now all the Fenrir are fascists, so if anything W5 is doubling down on the fascism-angle from previous editions. Now you have even more Sword of Heimdall than before in your WtA-game!</li> </ul>6) Okay... what you're describing isn't really a change. Before vampires were enemies because of what they did and their association with the Wyrm. Now they're enemies because of what they do, they're still the same antagonists they were in previous editions. It's not like the book listed some kind of &quot;Here's the vampire who works together with the Garou!&quot;-NPC in the book. I know the previews made some claims about changing the status of vampires in relation to Garou but the book we've got hasn't gone through with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) At least it makes it not that ugly.<br /> 2)OK, probably. Still no history there. Compare with old editions, where Garou could even assume what did difderent tribes do during Impergium. <br /> 3) Too vague. May be, may be not,highly (un)likely... Nothing happened there, folks. <br /> 4) So, Garou oral tradition is less solid that human one. As for the examples:<br /> *Invasion: Kinda &quot;our grand-grand-grand... parents were a part pf colonisation of Americas... like the rest of at least western world. It wasn't the good thing. <br /> Again, no -solid- history there.<br /> *Phillipine sept: yeah, it kinda happened, but not that tragic as genocide of the whole tribe/Fera sub-spice.<br /> *Fenrirs: Nevermind. ALL of them are antagonists now. What you can answer to anyone who point on the Fenrir history from old redactions.<br /> 6)&quot;Leechtalker Cities are full of the unquiet dead, blood-drinkers who play the world of the living against itself to their own benef i t. No surprise, then, that these Leeches are so often attached to the same agenda of avarice as the most short-sighted humans. The Leechtalker knows their pat-terns and their stink, and can root them out from their nests, given enough time and patience. But it\u2019s not always so simple; these deathless things don\u2019t seem to have spirits, and the Leeches know a lot about the cities where they reside. Sometimes a deal can be made.&quot; <br /> Leechtalker. Not leechhunter, not leechfinder. Garou kinda know that vampires are sneaky cruel bastards... and everyone including vampires themselves would agree with this stereotype. Yet no word about how they are Wyrm-beast or under 'Final Solution' in any other way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T11:20:54-08:00","id":1526769,"title":"","content":"I'm honestly not sure why you're giving W5 credit for &quot;removing&quot; these problematic elements and making Garou seem more like &quot;good guys&quot; when not only did it keep a lot of them and in several cases make them worse (Red Talons are now openly cannibalistic despite allowing homids! We don't need the Swords of Heimdall anymore because all Fenrir are fascist!), it also removed any sort of redeeming qualities or victories the Garou <i>did</i> have under their belts in favor of relentlessly shaming the player for wanting to play one. Not to mention that confronting these societal problems is part of the entire point and removing them takes out a good chunk of WtA's soul (for example, my mostly-disabled playgroup loves crinos-born because it's one of the few built-in confrontations of disability in TTRPGS, even if it's not perfect)<br /> <br /> And even then, it can't even commit to anything because every bit of worldbuilding is followed by &quot;oh but who knows for suuuure ooooo&quot; . So why even bother? It's an empty game made by people who actively dislike WtA only understand the way Vampire does things, and even then just barely. Werewolf fans want to play Werewolf, not a stripped down reskinned V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","user":"gh0st-fox","date":". 12-13-2023, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T12:08:46-08:00","id":1526770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526769#post1526769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly not sure why you're giving W5 credit for &quot;removing&quot; these problematic elements and making Garou seem more like &quot;good guys&quot; when not only did it keep a lot of them and in several cases make them worse (Red Talons are now openly cannibalistic despite allowing homids! We don't need the Swords of Heimdall anymore because all Fenrir are fascist!)</div> </div> </div> </div>And also every Garou that succumbs to hauglosk! What this game is telling us is to either give up or become Nazis, in essence. And that's fucked up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it also removed any sort of redeeming qualities or victories the Garou <i>did</i> have under their belts in favor of relentlessly shaming the player for wanting to play one. Not to mention that confronting these societal problems is part of the entire point and removing them takes out a good chunk of WtA's soul (for example, my mostly-disabled playgroup loves crinos-born because it's one of the few built-in confrontations of disability in TTRPGS, even if it's not perfect) </div> </div> </div>They could take a page or two from the ahi breed of the Nagah, or the shinju Kitsune. Some renaming, relaxing the sterility, decreasing their frequency (war form born have the same frequency as the human and serpent born Nagah) and they'd be good to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And even then, it can't even commit to anything because every bit of worldbuilding is followed by &quot;oh but who knows for suuuure ooooo&quot; . So why even bother? It's an empty game made by people who actively dislike WtA only understand the way Vampire does things, and even then just barely. Werewolf fans want to play Werewolf, not a stripped down reskinned V5. </div> </div> </div>And also tinged with cowardly corporate non-action. It's very similar to why Hasbro and WotC will never let Dark Sun get refurbished and re-released - it would take work they don't want to do, and the ones higher up on the corporate chain are the Sorcerer Kings, basically, and take great offense to being implicated in ruining the world (but they totally did).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T15:20:13-08:00","id":1526777,"title":"","content":"The biggest issue with W5 is that Forsaken did pretty much everything it tries to do better. The next biggest issues are the tracing and potentially unintentional cultural insensitivity, but I've not read the book enough to comment on those (spend \u00a350 to read it? Ha!).<br /> <br /> I do want to zoom in on the oral tradition though, because do you know who also had one? Why it's both the pre-W5 Group and the Uratha, and they were pretty accurate. The Garou had a good idea of their successes, failures, and the rules of the world they live in. Meanwhile the Uratha are wrong on several details but they're pretty bloody accurate when it comes to what Pangaea was actually like. There's still a lot of wiggle room and uncertainty if you dig into it, but they had their history and owned their glories and failings (and for the Forsaken the death of Father Wolf was both).<br /> <br /> The W5 Garou not only don't know, they're also seemingly the only ones who don't. Did the Corax write everything down and then share it with everybody but the PC faction? Or do we have to admit that oral traditions can be reliable, and the Garou's was not due to game writer fiat?<br /> <br /> Both the Garou and Uratha fucked everything up in the past. Pre-W5 the Garou gritted their teeth, said 'no I am right', and soldiered on, only later looking back to say 'no I was wrong, and I will atone by doing my duty' (I'm being very rough here). The Uratha decided that if they had destroyed Pangaea they were either going to fix this one way or another.<br /> <br /> The W5 Garou are more 'we did what? Why did nobody tell us we did that'. That's less interesting than any of the three groups that preceded them.<br /> <br /> The Garou are flawed. The Garou were always flawed. It is our flaws that make us human, and our struggle to do better than makes us great.<br /> <br /> The Garou Nation, like the Imperium of Man, is a steaming pile of shit. It's also more interesting to explore than a group of good guys.<br /> <br /> WtA had issues, and due to its subject matter and way it was designed it will always have issues. That's not to say that the designers can't strive to do better with the same material, but it feels like W5 didn't want to deal with those issues.<br /> <br /> Also I want to touch on Crinos, because I really like them, they're my favourite breed.<br /> <br /> Crinos were looked down on for their deformities and disabilities (and infertility). For all it's issues that's holding up a light to a very real and important issue in our society, and it's one that has not gone away. They also touch on the different ways parents are treated based on their gender, and other topics I'm really not qualified to discuss.<br /> <br /> Sure, I can still play a wheelchair bound Garou in W5, but the Crinos made our treatment of people with similar conditions an important part of the game. Let's not pretend that our society is now perfect when it comes to this, or any issue.<br /> <br /> We were told that W5 was no longer our world but darker, but rather just our world. I would like to suggest that it's actually painted over the cracks to present 'our world but brighter'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T23:23:11-08:00","id":1526795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526761#post1526761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) The War of Rage happened in W5. From pg 284: &quot;The Garou wish they knew, for it might make interacting with these other shapechangers less volatile. Sometimes, other shifters indicate that some long-ago grudge shaped the relationship the Garou have with them today \u2014 which would certainly be in keeping with today\u2019s Garou bearing the responsibility of past times of legend.&quot; The only weird part is that the Garou have somehow completely forgotten that this has happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one makes sense to me. The Garou weren't proud of what they did and so they just stopped telling the story of how they slaughtered all of the other shifters. Modern Garou have never heard any stories about a War of Rage and have no idea that it ever occurred let alone what role the werewolves played in it. Meanwhile with the other Shifters, the story of how the werewolves almost wiped them out gets handed down every generation and is probably the most important story that gets told. Ultimately within Garou society, the story of the War of Rage is likely known to a handful of Galliards who don't really spread it around (because they probably wouldn't be believed anyway) and maybe a few Children of Gaia (who have heard about it from other Shapeshifters).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526761#post1526761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Swords of Heimdall: Well, now all the Fenrir are fascists, so if anything W5 is doubling down on the fascism-angle from previous editions. Now you have even more Sword of Heimdall than before in your WtA-game!</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Fenrir are all Swords of Heimdall all the time so I don't see how if someone didn't like the Swords of Heimdall in the previous editions, they'd like what happened with the Fenrir in the new edition. Instead of being a rogue camp that was exterminated, the Swords basically took over the Fenrir in W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 12-14-2023, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T01:23:39-08:00","id":1526797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526795#post1526795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one makes sense to me. The Garou weren't proud of what they did and so they just stopped telling the story of how they slaughtered all of the other shifters. Modern Garou have never heard any stories about a War of Rage and have no idea that it ever occurred let alone what role the werewolves played in it. Meanwhile with the other Shifters, the story of how the werewolves almost wiped them out gets handed down every generation and is probably the most important story that gets told. Ultimately within Garou society, the story of the War of Rage is likely known to a handful of Galliards who don't really spread it around (because they probably wouldn't be believed anyway) and maybe a few Children of Gaia (who have heard about it from others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a massive change from 'Legacy' where the majority of Garou acknowledged that it was a mistake though their reaction from that point ranged from ' spilled milk' right down to trying to bring the lost Fera back by various means. And even those who didn't think it was a mistake still disagreed on whether parts of it were necessary or deserved and/or whether there was any point to trying to find out the reasons or triggers.<br /> <br /> Which seems more realistic to me. If the Coggies, Furies etc. thought it a terrible crime why would they not keep its memory alive and if others thought it a great victory over their corrupted brethren why would they not sing of their triumph?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T03:18:07-08:00","id":1526798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526795#post1526795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Fenrir are all Swords of Heimdall all the time so I don't see how if someone didn't like the Swords of Heimdall in the previous editions, they'd like what happened with the Fenrir in the new edition. Instead of being a rogue camp that was exterminated, the Swords basically took over the Fenrir in W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>As somebody who has no issue with the SoH being alive as a fringe element of the Fenrir, the W5 Cult of Fenris is stupid, not even reflective of what the Get were meant to satarise, and honestly quite insulting. That's not to say that the majority of the Get becoming overzealous extremists is a bad plot point, just that it didn't need to involve them all joining a camp which is practically on death's door when it's not six feet under.<br /> <br /> The W5 Get could have been really good, but instead of looking at toxic masculinity through a more modern perspective, or any of their other themes, in favour of a rather hamfisted attack on fascism.<br /> <br /> But we should have seen this coming when the Weaver aligned aspects of the Glass Walkers became their focus instead of a result of them being <i>adaptable</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T06:04:05-08:00","id":1526803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526797#post1526797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which seems more realistic to me. If the Coggies, Furies etc. thought it a terrible crime why would they not keep its memory alive and if others thought it a great victory over their corrupted brethren why would they not sing of their triumph?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's what they did in the legacy editions. In W5, the War of Rage was a source of shame so they didn't discuss it. After a few generations the event was mostly forgotten. If younger generations knew what had happened, maybe they would sing songs about it, but they lack the knowledge to do so. That is something that happens - stories, sometimes even important ones get lost as the older generations that knew it didn't talk about it with the younger generations. Even with writing and modern information storage this is still something that you can see occurring in certain places.<br /> <br /> Look at the difference between Japan and Germany when it comes to general knowledge of WW2 crimes. In Germany there's a strong pressure to teach the younger generations what Germany did during WW2. They learn all about it in school, so most Germans are familiar at least with the general points of what crimes against humanity their country committed during WW2. Meanwhile in Japan, that's not the case at all. Children in school typically aren't taught the details of the brutality that Japan inflicted in Korea or in China or other places. The average citizen (especially younger people) has a vague understanding along the lines of, &quot;Yeah, we did some bad stuff, but everyone was doing bad things, even the United States, we had nuclear weapons dropped on us, and then we apologized for everything we did, so why are people still angry about it? Nobody is mad at Germany. Korea, China and everyone else needs to get over it already.&quot;<br /> <br /> In school, most Japanese people don't learn about what Unit 731 did. And in those textbooks that describe the Korean Comfort Women, it usually identifies them as &quot;mostly&quot; prostitutes who were willingly selling sexual services to soldiers. The real knowledge of what Japan did is largely confined to specific college classes or historical books, and aren't things that most of the citizens are familiar with.<br /> <br /> Ultimately if events aren't actively discussed and taught, they'll fall out of common knowledge in just a couple of generations. WW2 was 80 years ago, the War of Rage was 8000+ years ago. It doesn't strike me as weird of strange that by the modern day, the vast majority of Garou would never even have heard about it or know about it.<br /> <br /> Note that I do think it plays even harder into the &quot;everything sucks and nothing you can do matters&quot; aspect of W5. In the Legacy edition, trying to make amends for the War of Rage and bring the shapeshifters back together was a legendary task. In W5 it's essentially impossible because most Garou don't even know it happened. So before they can apologize to the other Shifters and try to make up for the wrongs, first they have to realize it even happened, then decide that it was a bad thing, and then try to convince the rest of the Garou nation what happened and then convince them that they need to apologize.<br /> <br /> I suspect that even if they did find out it happened, and believed it happened, most Garou would say, &quot;It happened 8000 years ago. Why am I supposed to apologize for that? Those other shapeshifters need to get it over it already.&quot;<br /> <br /> You heard a lot of white people in the US recently saying the same thing about the Tulsa Race Massacre when still-living victims who were directly injured went to court to seek amends. &quot;It happened so long ago, nobody around today should be considered responsible.&quot; <br /> <br /> So to be clear, it's not a change I like, but it's one that I feel makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 12-14-2023, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T07:16:36-08:00","id":1526808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526795#post1526795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one makes sense to me. The Garou weren't proud of what they did and so they just stopped telling the story of how they slaughtered all of the other shifters. Modern Garou have never heard any stories about a War of Rage and have no idea that it ever occurred let alone what role the werewolves played in it. Meanwhile with the other Shifters, the story of how the werewolves almost wiped them out gets handed down every generation and is probably the most important story that gets told. Ultimately within Garou society, the story of the War of Rage is likely known to a handful of Galliards who don't really spread it around (because they probably wouldn't be believed anyway) and maybe a few Children of Gaia (who have heard about it from other Shapeshifters).</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue for me is that what you're describing is you adding to what the book offers. It's a problem similar to the Stargazer-section. There it says: &quot;That said, none know the Patron Spirit granting its boon to the Stargazers. In the past, Chimera bestowed favor upon the tribe, but that great spirit seems to have amicably parted ways with the Stargazers \u2014 or so it seems to those Garou who interpret such things.&quot; And there's the same problem: How does no one know who the Stargazers Patron-Spirit is? Has anybody asked them? &quot;No one knows and the only thing the other Garou know is that it isn't Chimera anymore.&quot; You would only need one more short sentence saying something like &quot;The Garou tried to talk to the Stargazers about it but they remain tight-lipped and act very secretive when asked questions.&quot;<br /> <br /> And it's the same with the War of Rage. Other Shifters are unfriendly, they say it's because of a conflict between them and the Garou in the distant past and the Garou are... what? It would make more sense if you either removed the hint of the War of Rage or added a short comment on the Garou-stance. Like you mentioned, maybe Garou have stopped sharing the tales about the War of Rage or it's now considered &quot;secret knowledge&quot; and only high-Renown Garou get to hear the stories.<br /> <br /> It's these half-formed ideas whose logic only makes sense if you start to bring in your own ideas. Like trying to fill a plothole but for worldbuilding. But this isn't how lore/worldbuilding should work. You want to set up mysteries because they raise interesting questions that can be answered through play. Or you set up elements in the setting that can be used as a plothook. But the process shouldn't start with the first step being &quot;Okay, let me think about how I get this bit to make sense.&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T15:41:38-08:00","id":1526818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526803#post1526803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what they did in the legacy editions. In W5, the War of Rage was a source of shame so they didn't discuss it. After a few generations the event was mostly forgotten. If younger generations knew what had happened, maybe they would sing songs about it, but they lack the knowledge to do so. That is something that happens - stories, sometimes even important ones get lost as the older generations that knew it didn't talk about it with the younger generations. Even with writing and modern information storage this is still something that you can see occurring in certain places.<br /> <br /> Look at the difference between Japan and Germany when it comes to general knowledge of WW2 crimes. In Germany there's a strong pressure to teach the younger generations what Germany did during WW2. They learn all about it in school, so most Germans are familiar at least with the general points of what crimes against humanity their country committed during WW2. Meanwhile in Japan, that's not the case at all. Children in school typically aren't taught the details of the brutality that Japan inflicted in Korea or in China or other places. The average citizen (especially younger people) has a vague understanding along the lines of, &quot;Yeah, we did some bad stuff, but everyone was doing bad things, even the United States, we had nuclear weapons dropped on us, and then we apologized for everything we did, so why are people still angry about it? Nobody is mad at Germany. Korea, China and everyone else needs to get over it already.&quot;<br /> <br /> In school, most Japanese people don't learn about what Unit 731 did. And in those textbooks that describe the Korean Comfort Women, it usually identifies them as &quot;mostly&quot; prostitutes who were willingly selling sexual services to soldiers. The real knowledge of what Japan did is largely confined to specific college classes or historical books, and aren't things that most of the citizens are familiar with.<br /> <br /> Ultimately if events aren't actively discussed and taught, they'll fall out of common knowledge in just a couple of generations. WW2 was 80 years ago, the War of Rage was 8000+ years ago. It doesn't strike me as weird of strange that by the modern day, the vast majority of Garou would never even have heard about it or know about it.<br /> <br /> Note that I do think it plays even harder into the &quot;everything sucks and nothing you can do matters&quot; aspect of W5. In the Legacy edition, trying to make amends for the War of Rage and bring the shapeshifters back together was a legendary task. In W5 it's essentially impossible because most Garou don't even know it happened. So before they can apologize to the other Shifters and try to make up for the wrongs, first they have to realize it even happened, then decide that it was a bad thing, and then try to convince the rest of the Garou nation what happened and then convince them that they need to apologize.<br /> <br /> I suspect that even if they did find out it happened, and believed it happened, most Garou would say, &quot;It happened 8000 years ago. Why am I supposed to apologize for that? Those other shapeshifters need to get it over it already.&quot;<br /> <br /> You heard a lot of white people in the US recently saying the same thing about the Tulsa Race Massacre when still-living victims who were directly injured went to court to seek amends. &quot;It happened so long ago, nobody around today should be considered responsible.&quot;<br /> <br /> So to be clear, it's not a change I like, but it's one that I feel makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>All this applies to humans, yes. Humans don't have a magical scoreboard for their fame among their people kept up by a multitude of allied spirits, however, and as far as we know, don't have ancestor spirits that will show up to yank you by the ear if they think that you're disrespecting them egregiously. Garou, on the other hand, have both, which is part of why they kept singing the triumph of the War of Rage over the dirty, Wyrm-consorting Gurahl and their dubious allies among the other Fera (but the Corax spied for us so they're totally cool).<br /> <br /> Mechanically, taking a stand against the prevailing narrative of the War of Rage involves taking major hits to Honor Renown (declaring your ancestors to be in the wrong and the tale to be glorifying butchers is considered disrespecting your elders and yourself, and won't really be guaranteed to win you Glory or Wisdom, either) and potentially even alienating your ancestor-spirits, which means no backup via the Ancestors background. Some spirits might have also agreed to pacts against some of the Fera, and those are not lifted or changed lightly, or often, ever, so that's going to, at minimum, require some major deeds dedicated to patching up that relationship.<br /> <br /> And it's also hard to get over something for the other side when they also have ancestor-spirits with, shall we say, substantial differences in how the Garou posture, not to mention the Mokole, for whom the War of Rage was always just yesterday. They also know that there are some Fera that weren't so lucky, and so aren't inclined to trust the Garou on that basis as well; they might well just want to finish the job.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, if we were dealing with normal humans, without long memories, a secret culture, and not just actual but incredibly strong ancestral memories, you'd be correct. But that's not Werewolf: the Apocalypse, so we're back where we were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T16:03:32-08:00","id":1526820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526818#post1526818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All this applies to humans, yes. Humans don't have a magical scoreboard for their fame among their people kept up by a multitude of allied spirits, however, and as far as we know, don't have ancestor spirits that will show up to yank you by the ear if they think that you're disrespecting them egregiously. Garou, on the other hand, have both, which is part of why they kept singing the triumph of the War of Rage over the dirty, Wyrm-consorting Gurahl and their dubious allies among the other Fera (but the Corax spied for us so they're totally cool).<br /> <br /> Mechanically, taking a stand against the prevailing narrative of the War of Rage involves taking major hits to Honor Renown (declaring your ancestors to be in the wrong and the tale to be glorifying butchers is considered disrespecting your elders and yourself, and won't really be guaranteed to win you Glory or Wisdom, either) and potentially even alienating your ancestor-spirits, which means no backup via the Ancestors background. Some spirits might have also agreed to pacts against some of the Fera, and those are not lifted or changed lightly, or often, ever, so that's going to, at minimum, require some major deeds dedicated to patching up that relationship.<br /> <br /> And it's also hard to get over something for the other side when they also have ancestor-spirits with, shall we say, substantial differences in how the Garou posture, not to mention the Mokole, for whom the War of Rage was always just yesterday. They also know that there are some Fera that weren't so lucky, and so aren't inclined to trust the Garou on that basis as well; they might well just want to finish the job.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, if we were dealing with normal humans, without long memories, a secret culture, and not just actual but incredibly strong ancestral memories, you'd be correct. But that's not Werewolf: the Apocalypse, so we're back where we were.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they will justify it with the removal of the umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T18:46:12-08:00","id":1526824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526820#post1526820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they will justify it with the removal of the umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we've already seen what W5 served up and we know it sucks, not the least reasons of which is the lack of an Ancestors background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T21:19:48-08:00","id":1526827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526818#post1526818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All this applies to humans, yes. Humans don't have a magical scoreboard for their fame among their people kept up by a multitude of allied spirits, however, and as far as we know, don't have ancestor spirits that will show up to yank you by the ear if they think that you're disrespecting them egregiously. Garou, on the other hand, have both, which is part of why they kept singing the triumph of the War of Rage over the dirty, Wyrm-consorting Gurahl and their dubious allies among the other Fera (but the Corax spied for us so they're totally cool).<br /> <br /> Mechanically, taking a stand against the prevailing narrative of the War of Rage involves taking major hits to Honor Renown (declaring your ancestors to be in the wrong and the tale to be glorifying butchers is considered disrespecting your elders and yourself, and won't really be guaranteed to win you Glory or Wisdom, either) and potentially even alienating your ancestor-spirits, which means no backup via the Ancestors background. Some spirits might have also agreed to pacts against some of the Fera, and those are not lifted or changed lightly, or often, ever, so that's going to, at minimum, require some major deeds dedicated to patching up that relationship.<br /> <br /> And it's also hard to get over something for the other side when they also have ancestor-spirits with, shall we say, substantial differences in how the Garou posture, not to mention the Mokole, for whom the War of Rage was always just yesterday. They also know that there are some Fera that weren't so lucky, and so aren't inclined to trust the Garou on that basis as well; they might well just want to finish the job.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, if we were dealing with normal humans, without long memories, a secret culture, and not just actual but incredibly strong ancestral memories, you'd be correct. But that's not Werewolf: the Apocalypse, so we're back where we were.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was 8000+ years ago. You don't have to openly reject the people who engaged in the War of Rage, it's just a matter of the tribal storytellers choosing to not not talk about it until over the course of millennium people don't know about it anymore. My earlier point was that even in human society with massive written records, and video records, and people who are still living who can attest to events, you can still have major events fall out of general knowledge and circulation within just a generation or two of them happening. With the Garou we're talking 300+ generations removed from the War of Rage and the modern era. Even with magic, if at some point, tribal storytellers decided to stop to passing on the story of the War of Rage, it's pretty plausible to me that it could have succeeded over that timeframe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T21:28:07-08:00","id":1526828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526827#post1526827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was 8000+ years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, again, thanks to ancestral memory, it was basically yesterday.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't have to openly reject the people who engaged in the War of Rage, it's just a matter of the tribal storytellers choosing to not not talk about it until over the course of millennium people don't know about it anymore. </div> </div> </div>Which is considered to be a grave insult to the Garou in question. This is how their culture works - not telling tales about them is making a stand against them, personally. Not believing in the spirit of their boasting is a stand against them. This is why it's so incredibly difficult for the Garou to change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My earlier point was that even in human society with massive written records, and video records, and people who are still living who can attest to events, you can still have major events fall out of general knowledge and circulation within just a generation or two of them happening. With the Garou we're talking 300+ generations removed from the War of Rage and the modern era. Even with magic, if at some point, tribal storytellers decided to stop to passing on the story of the War of Rage, it's pretty plausible to me that it could have succeeded over that timeframe. </div> </div> </div>They didn't. They wouldn't. It's not how they work. No matter how terrible, it's even etched into the fucking <i>Silver Record</i>. It's part of their main canon of stories. W5 ignoring it is part of why it's a shitty excuse for a W:tA edition that doesn't know what it's supposed to be about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T22:07:37-08:00","id":1526829,"title":"","content":"Oh, I see the disagreement. You're talking about legacy editions with stuff like Ancestral Memory and such that doesn't exist in W5,, while I'm just talking about W5.<br /> <br /> To me, purely within the scope of W5, it seems plausible that certain stories, even important ones, could have fallen out of collective memory.<br /> <br /> Please don't think I'm suggesting importing this into the legacy editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 12-15-2023, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T22:49:10-08:00","id":1526831,"title":"","content":"You're not talking about what's purely W5 though. You're assuming it was vastly long ago, when W5 has done it's best to ensure there's no set time-frame to any of this. W5's setup is that the conflict between the Garou and the other shifters could have been 50,000 years ago, or 50 days ago, but the Garou don't know what happened because the book presents their ability to generate cultural knowledge as being that shitty under the design excuse of giving more freedom to adjust the setting to taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T23:13:10-08:00","id":1526832,"title":"","content":"Something I noticed about this post on reddit is how it damns with faint praise. It doesn't really like w5 it just dislikes werewolf in previous editions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T23:36:35-08:00","id":1526833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526832#post1526832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I noticed about this post on reddit is how it damns with faint praise. It doesn't really like w5 it just dislikes werewolf in previous editions</div> </div> </div> </div>I've noticed similar, including some... choice memes about Red Talons and the Fenrir. Generally, WtA is seen as racist,facist,anti-human and including bestiality. So, I guess W5 would sound good in that context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T00:00:46-08:00","id":1526834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526831#post1526831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not talking about what's purely W5 though. You're assuming it was vastly long ago, when W5 has done it's best to ensure there's no set time-frame to any of this. W5's setup is that the conflict between the Garou and the other shifters could have been 50,000 years ago, or 50 days ago, but the Garou don't know what happened because the book presents their ability to generate cultural knowledge as being that shitty under the design excuse of giving more freedom to adjust the setting to taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reading the text and coming away with the idea that the conflict between werewolves and the other shifters happened so long ago that it has fallen out of general knowledge because, for whatever reason (maybe shame?) the werewolves did not want to pass down the story of their deeds. That seems like something that could plausibly happen to me.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sometimes, other shifters indicate that some long-ago grudge shaped the relationship the Garou have with them today \u2014 which would certainly be in keeping with today\u2019s Garou bearing the responsibility of past times of legend.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not sure how you could read that line about &quot;past times of legend&quot; and come away thinking it means within living memory, let alone something like a few dozen days ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T01:16:43-08:00","id":1526835,"title":"","content":"Because the text is brimming with examples of the Garou not knowing things within not only living memory, but recent history. Entering the Age of Apocalypse is a &quot;time of legend&quot; than supposedly just happened (or maybe not and the Garou were just deluding themselves that it hadn't started already... because that's how W5 frames everything).<br /> <br /> Going just on the text of W5 there's no frame of reference for what &quot;times of legend&quot; are, and how frequently they happen. We have no idea how a raven-shifter views &quot;long ago&quot; relative to the Garou's own ability to maintain their histories. You don't have anything coming strictly from the W5 text to tell me definitively that the long ago past times of legend all didn't happen in the last 50 years because that's just how the shifters view history and time. The Garou struggle with history of things that happened right before the Garou Nation went to shit as meaningful organization... which supposedly happened within the recent history of the default PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T02:12:20-08:00","id":1526838,"title":"","content":"I feel like the implication is that the conflict between werewolves and other shifters happened a long-ass time ago in the distant past. And to me, if we're looking at a long enough temporal distance, then it's plausible that knowledge of that event could have fallen out Garou culture. <br /> <br /> Obviously if that conflict happened last week, that would be pretty stupid, but I don't feel the text really pushes that particular interpretation. <br /> <br /> There are a lot of issues with W5, but I don't think that the the general loss of knowledge of an ancient event is one of them. Now knowing more recent things is very problematic, but I don't think that's what's happening in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T02:48:25-08:00","id":1526841,"title":"","content":"And you've all but acknowledged that it's not the text, it's your interpretation of the things to purposefully make it as good as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T03:09:14-08:00","id":1526842,"title":"","content":"I feel like that's even more true for you. If you interpret &quot;long ago&quot; and &quot;time of legend&quot; as a few months or years rather than centuries or millennium then yeah, it's completely nonsensical. Meanwhile I feel like it's pretty obvious the intent of those lines l was to position this conflict so far in the past that many werewolves don't even know it happened.<br /> <br /> It just seems bizarre that someone would read that and their takeaway was that this conflict must have happened days or months before. I feel like to some degree, people are intentionally running with the least charitable interpreration of every line in the book tgey can come up with in order to better justify their dislike of it.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of W5 but there are parts I think are interesting or neat or that are reasonable within the context of a new and different game. There also a bunch of dumb shit in there too. This singular issue seems plausible and reasonable to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T03:36:04-08:00","id":1526843,"title":"","content":"It's not &quot;true&quot; for me, because you're trying to reframe my statements as if I'm trying to debate when an event in W5 &quot;really&quot; happened. My position is that W5 - purposefully because they said so and I don't need to make shit up about what other posters are thinking and then weasel word it to try not to sound like an ass even though it just makes you sound worse - doesn't give a set time frame for any of this. It's supposed to work whenever the group want it to work. But that doesn't work because there's not dials for thing like how much the Garou know based on how long ago it was. They know jack shit about stuff equally regardless of distant ancient past, or literally according to the text stuff that's happened in the last decade.<br /> <br /> You insisting it has to be ancient history is <b>you contradicting the text</b>. The book doesn't say the Garou don't know because it's lost to the fog pre-history. The book just says they don't have a clue (as it does on many, many topics). When or even if it actually happened is a mystery, and they said on social media there intention isn't to elaborate on that kind of world building.<br /> <br /> You find it interesting because you're filling in a gap with answers that you find interesting (because you're doing that, nothing in the book says anything about the Garou purposefully suppressing knowledge of the past, you made that up because it's a cool idea to explore, and it would be even cooler with a game that had more respect for the legacy material where there's actually complexity to the idea of trying to hide the past when there are beings around that can reveal it anyway). That is, in effect, what the W5 developers want groups to do. The problem is that what they did set in stone in the text is only sensible if your group decides on a much smaller set on possible answers than the game implies you should be able to.<br /> <br /> I don't need to read things uncharitably. The book purposefully is as vague as possible with the game's lore. Since it neither wants to engage in world building, nor does it want to engage in providing tools to guide groups to do their own world building by exploring the implications of different answers to things they have purposefully left undefined, it's a flawed product. It doesn't matter if you can come up with some neat stuff despite that. That's just a Rule Zero argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T03:41:50-08:00","id":1526845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526833#post1526833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've noticed similar, including some... choice memes about Red Talons and the Fenrir. Generally, WtA is seen as racist,facist,anti-human and including bestiality. So, I guess W5 would sound good in that context.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there's some truth to the racism (mostly unintentional in trying to be inclusive without involving the people themselves), and WtA's relationship with fascism is complicated. I don't think anybody here would deny that the legacy editions have their issues.<br /> <br /> The problem as I see it is 1) W5 runs so far into the other direction that it hits the same issues (except now instead of <s>fascists</s> the religious right we're playing people who can't be too passionate about their cause), and 2) throwing out the baby with the bathwater. An important appeal of WtA is that you can be effective by violently disrupting the groups behind environmental destruction while the kinfolk do the grunt work, that while your Rage is causing you issues it is also a righteous fury that will carry you to victory. That in a darker world where the divine protectors abuse their kids for being born wrong and your copy of Revenant: the Charade might contain a literal evil spirit the flames are burning ever so slightly brighter.<br /> <br /> There are also parts of legacy WtA that weren't problematic but are potentially uncomfortable realistic. The treatment of metis, the uncaring scale of your opposition, the fact your elders just don't want to adapt to the times. Even the fact that your parents and elders will have very strong views on who you're sleeping with.<br /> <br /> W20 broke the current trend of saying 'th world will accept your character's by going 'no, sometimes the Garou will not accept someone as they are' when discussing transgender werewolves and the lengths they go to while still being denied acceptance. This is great, but is something W5 will never dare to do (it's more likely to declare trans Garou have their bodies changed upon First Change). I personally love Forsaken's 'fuck you gender binary' gift, but there's also value in playing out your society being a bunch of x-phobic twats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T07:30:18-08:00","id":1526848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526845#post1526845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W20 broke the current trend of saying 'th world will accept your character's by going 'no, sometimes the Garou will not accept someone as they are' when discussing transgender werewolves and the lengths they go to while still being denied acceptance. This is great, but is something W5 will never dare to do (it's more likely to declare trans Garou have their bodies changed upon First Change). I personally love Forsaken's 'fuck you gender binary' gift, but there's also value in playing out your society being a bunch of x-phobic twats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree. While I can totally see some Furies or Walkers having issues, you have to remember that garou are not Judeo-Christian. Homosexuality exists in nature and in a culture so strongly tied to nature spirits, even changing gender would not be judged outside very humanized circles.<br /> <br /> But W5 takes away not only the nature but the very concept of animism itself from WtA. The garou of W5 are discouraged from forming ties with spirits by the mechanics and the fact that they can only choose tribal patrons as pack patrons. Spirits cannot be touchstones and even wolves are HEAVILY discouraged.<br /> <br /> WtA was a game that looked beyond humanity and showed how our actions hurt everything around us. W5 is firmly tied to humanity and any deviation or effort to connect to nature are treated as rare or unwanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":".  patrons not totems 12-15-2023, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T08:40:59-08:00","id":1526852,"title":"","content":"Plus, that whole &quot;Gaia doesn't make mistakes!&quot; BS was entirely due to PDX meddling, i.e. it's BS from the current crop of folks in charge, so it doesn't really count as W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T14:30:35-08:00","id":1526875,"title":"","content":"This may be a bit sudden, but did the Silent striders change their name in W5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T14:50:56-08:00","id":1526878,"title":"","content":"Um... I don't think so? They were the Silent Strides in the old books, and W5 still calls them that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T14:58:50-08:00","id":1526879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526875#post1526875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be a bit sudden, but did the Silent striders change their name in W5?</div> </div> </div> </div>They still have the same name, are kinda the same but with the patented W5-charm of &quot;Who knows&quot;. This is how they're introduced: &quot;Among wolves, Garou follow where prey leads the pack, and among humans, Garou have historically been found in cultures that are either migratory or diasporic. Deep in their own history, the Silent Striders were themselves\u2026 cursed? by a powerful spirit, malignant and not wholly understood, and as a result they often find sympathetic peoples and familiar practices among ever-moving or dispersed cultures.&quot; The Silent Striders are still nomadic and cursed but in W5 they have absolutely no idea by who and why. And as you see from the quote even the &quot;curse&quot;-part gets a question-mark in W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T15:07:39-08:00","id":1526880,"title":"","content":"Anyone noticed how it completely it fails to discuss usage of violence in environmentalism in a period where its becoming increasingly possible that its on the cards as the situation degenerates?<br /> this seems particularly damning considering old school werewolves were ecoterrorists and the get doing that is frowned on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-16-2023, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T15:14:16-08:00","id":1526881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526842#post1526842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like that's even more true for you. If you interpret &quot;long ago&quot; and &quot;time of legend&quot; as a few months or years rather than centuries or millennium then yeah, it's completely nonsensical. Meanwhile I feel like it's pretty obvious the intent of those lines l was to position this conflict so far in the past that many werewolves don't even know it happened.<br /> <br /> It just seems bizarre that someone would read that and their takeaway was that this conflict must have happened days or months before. I feel like to some degree, people are intentionally running with the least charitable interpreration of every line in the book tgey can come up with in order to better justify their dislike of it.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of W5 but there are parts I think are interesting or neat or that are reasonable within the context of a new and different game. There also a bunch of dumb shit in there too. This singular issue seems plausible and reasonable to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the underlying issue here is, it <i>would</i> be an interesting thing to address... if the corebook didn't feel like it was doing a big sweep under the rug. To address both sides of this argument:<br /> <br /> 1. Getting rid of ancestor spirits and how the Nation addresses its sins feels like it's removing a huge chunk of history, hubris, and reckoning that was central to the Nation in Legacy editions. It also opens up the territory to explore the War of Rage from multiple perspectives, and create the kind of scenario where proud images of the Wild West and Manifest Destiny and California elementary school projects on the mission system give way to the Apache Wars and the reservation schools. It feels like it opens the door for a more fractured Nation, where the Children of Gaia might have tried to find out what happened and actually gotten a better perspective from the Fera, and the more traditional tribes take the &quot;that was millennia ago&quot; approach, and some real reactionaries act like those folks on Twitter who respond to &quot;Happy Indigenous Peoples Day&quot; by saying &quot;Yeah well the Aztecs ate people!&quot; <br /> 2. But, as the book stands, there is no room for shame or doubt or debate because the proud legacy of the Garou Nation is <i>gone. </i>Your characters don't know shit, and it's heavily implied their mentors don't know shit. The Impergium doesn't have a historical record beyond &quot;it was bad, we think,&quot; the collapse of the Nation itself is hard to date, and some tribes have no idea of their foundational lore beyond conjecture. There are artifacts and spiritual pacts and debts, but you're a people without a clear history. It's Posadism with fewer dolphins. All you really know about what came before you is it didn't work, your ancestors were assholes, and you need to do something new.<br /> 3. Which is where the Fera come in. There's a good possibility that you may need to make amends with these other shifters for sins past. But you don't know what those sins <i>are</i>. Part of that is historical erasure, but there's not really a counternarrative to push against, no sense that you'll be accused of &quot;critical shifter theory&quot; if you argue that, hey, maybe we should make up for that genocide we did. <br /> <br /> That's my issue with how the W5 corebook lays it out, though I acknowledge future books could correct it. It's ladling on the message of &quot;Your ancestors were shit,&quot; but when it comes time to address the concrete sins that you need to correct, it often adopts an air of &quot;Who knows, we're not telling.&quot; You can't talk to the Fera because they're snippy (for good reason) and you've got nothing to go on. It's not about providing the materials for redress by staring down your sins; rather, it feels like the boogeyman version of addressing racial injustice in the historical record, where some DEI scholar tells your kid, &quot;Your great-grandpa was racist, and that stain passes on to you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28234-justincognito","name":"JustinCognito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T15:53:58-08:00","id":1526883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526880#post1526880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone noticed how it completely it fails to discuss usage of violence in environmentalism in a period where its becoming increasingly possible that its on the cards as the situation degenerates?<br /> this seems particularly damning considering old school werewolves were ecoterrorists and the get doing that is friend on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, this is part of the erasure of nature in W5. For all the book yaps about being inclusive and considerate of Indigenous people, it gleefully discourages stewarding the land.<br /> <br /> The wanted PCs are suburban or urban youths who have little ties to anything outside cities and who are disconnected from their cultures. This could be a great starting point, but the book treats this disconnect as a GOOD thing.<br /> <br /> Actually doing something is either treated as insanity (CoF) or abstracted to the point that it is little more than a werewolfy HoA meeting.<br /> <br /> For all the flaws in Legacy, at least it has the guts to say pollution, colonialism and hunting keytstone species are bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 12-15-2023, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T16:13:31-08:00","id":1526884,"title":"","content":"Thinking about the discussions on history in Garou, I think the writing-team for the released W5 book didn\u2019t work with any sort of timeline or consideration for what happens when. So any mention of time is more a coincidence than a sign of intent, I would say. Take the Garou-Nation section on pg 37. It starts to outline the contours of the Garou-Nation as unknowable. When did it start? Who knows. When did it fall? Who knows? How long did it last? A decade? A century? Millenia? Who knows. Somehow nobody can be sure about that.<br /> <br /> More importantly, in the next paragraph, though, suddenly a time-frame for the decline of the Garou-Nation is introduced: &quot;The Wyrm\u2019s growing strength manifested through numerous tools, and through agents who goaded many werewolves into participating in colonial conquest by imperial powers, which tapped the Garou\u2019s inherent love for dominance. At times, these agents took advantage of the uncertainty brought about by the Renaissance, the Enlightenment, and the Industrial Revolution.&quot; So the time-frame it's talking about is roughly 15th century to 19th. That\u2019s already a contradiction of the first paragraph. The section started with all these unknowable facts and then immediately afterward jumped into \u201cLet me tell you about the age of colonization and what the Garou did during that period.\u201d<br /> <br /> Two other interesting bits here: Why do we start with the Renaissance here? It's unclear why that particular time-frame is even picked. Maybe it's because of the &quot;capitalocene era&quot; bit from the first chapter but it's poor writing to not connect the dots here. If the writers were willing to throw around terms like &quot;capitalocene&quot;, the least one could expect them to do is back that up. Sadly the W5 corebook underwhelms in that regard. It doesn't seem like a lot of thought was put into the worldbuilding here. And the second point is that it's telling how the description uses European history-periods for the description. The links between Tribes and human culture/ethnicity were erased, the Native American Tribes' identity was removed but look at that, it goes right back to the default of viewing history through the lens of Europe.<br /> <br /> Then the next paragraph offers examples of Garou's bad behavior, the invasion of America, the killing of that Sept of witch-wolves... So far so good, it fits within that time-frame of colonialism that was mentioned before... But here comes the kicker: The third event that is mentioned in the same paragraph is... the fall of the White Howlers and them turning into the Black Spiral Dancers.<br /> <br /> The weirdness of the White Howlers being mentioned in this context aside and what this means for the W5 chronology of events, think about this: It\u2019s the age of colonialism, the bad deeds of Garou are the invasion of America and eradicating a Sept of witch-wolves in South-East Asia. I get that there are criticisms to be levied against past editions in terms of diverse representation but this feels <i>like a step backwards</i>. After all, what the Garou-Nation section in W5 outlines is a perspective firmly focused on white Europeans conquering the world. And the victims of these bad actions are merely victims/targets. At least, with previous editions the perspective of the Native American Tribes offered a different perspective. Now it\u2019s just guilt over European Garou doing bad stuff.<br /> <br /> They\u2019ve removed the Native American Tribes only to recenter the whole thing from a European colonialist perspective. Sure, it\u2019s a perspective tinged with guilt and regret but it speaks volumes that the retrospective on colonialism as a bad thing gets representation while the representation of Indigenous voices reacting to it and/or suffering because of it was erased.<br /> <br /> I think James F. Sambrano was right in calling this game being about \u201cwhite guilt\u201d. There\u2019s no global or historical perspective here. It\u2019s just present-day white people awkwardly trying to wrangle with the bad stuff of the past and the present. It\u2019s all about being angry at what has happened in the past and how ugly the present is. It\u2019s bad. But then there\u2019s no plan on how to make things better. Because &quot;feeling bad for what was and how things are&quot; is all you get from the limited horizons of the W5 corebook's writing-team. The book just continuously looks for affirmation about what is considered bad and ugly. The past of the Garou is bad and the W5 corebook will NEVER let you move on from that. No matter where you are in the book, at some point, you return to \u201cBut do you know that the Garou are bad\u2026?\u201d. And the book shows little interest in the question of \u201cSo now what\u2026?\u201d. Or as the &quot;Drawing Distinctions&quot;-sidebar dismissively talks about fighting companies that advance climate-change: &quot;It's an emotional issue.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nobody expects the vampires of VtM to save the world but the Garou of WtA are on a holy mission by Gaia to prevent the Apocalypse. Since it\u2019s the World Of Darkness the Garou aren\u2019t very good at doing that. W5 doesn\u2019t really improve the formula by stripping away the nuance and focusing on \u201cGarou suck\u201d. Then add corporate-mandated \u201cstreet-level-only\u201d and \u201cless Umbra\u201d and you get\u2026 this. Diversity got repressed, you got a game focused on feeling bad and tons of lore/worldbuilding got stripped away to be replaced by nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T16:37:57-08:00","id":1526885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526883#post1526883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, this is part of the erasure of nature in W5. For all the book yaps about being inclusive and considerate of Indigenous people, it gleefully discourages stewarding the land.<br /> <br /> The wanted PCs are suburban or urban youths who have little ties to anything outside cities and who are disconnected from their cultures. This could be a great starting point, but the book treats this disconnect as a GOOD thing.<br /> <br /> Actually doing something is either treated as insanity (CoF) or abstracted to the point that it is little more than a werewolfy HoA meeting.<br /> <br /> For all the flaws in Legacy, at least it has the guts to say pollution, colonialism and hunting keytstone species are bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I remember Sambrano saying in his article he wanted the Gale Stalkers to be a group of land protectors inspired by Indigenous practices of land stewardship without necessarily being all Indigenous. Like the Standing Rock protesters inviting white people in as long as they didn't showboat. But Muammar's counterargument was this just made them a tribe full of Ahrouns doing what Garou are already supposed to be doing.<br /> <br /> In trying to divorce itself from inspiration in real-world cultural and spiritual practices out of a fear of fucking them up, the game has become culturally agnostic... and, as a result, a bit Western by default. It says not to fuck up any real world animist faiths but makes what the Garou have more of a system of patronage based on contracts and material gain (the idea of spirit Gifts in Legacy veered uncomfortably close to the idea that Native American spirituality has to have material effects to have meaning based on its &quot;more liminal&quot; nature, but it at least had a system of ancestor worship and a greater cosmology to interact with bound into it; now it feels like more of a vending machine). As mentioned by Knightingale, its attempts at addressing the sins of the past risk falling into a white guilt paradigm of the unquenchable sin that you must bear without necessarily knowing how to correct, like how some works of fiction act as if all natives stopped existing in the area past a certain year (which is unfortunately true in some cases, but not as many as you'd think).<br /> <br /> Even the sidebars meant to offer an Indigenous perspective fall into this a bit. The first one talks about generational trauma and how Indigenous communities still deal with the sense of loss that comes from exterminationist campaigns, broken treaties, the reservation school system, and other attempts at genocide, both cultural and physical... and then it says &quot;This might apply to the Garou as well.&quot; Problem 1: I can most likely go on a Dine reservation and still hear from somebody about Spider Grandmother and old bits of oral tradition, but I can't have a Silent Strider tell me why exactly their tribe is nomadic. Problem 2: This generational trauma stemmed from a campaign meant to either kill Indians or &quot;kill the Indian, save the man&quot;; what happened to the Garou to fuck up their sense of history even worse?<br /> <br /> The second sidebar, on the other hand, is all about how Western culture is future-oriented and materialistic, which can cause people to lose touch with their ancestral roots... and then, again, applies this to all Garou, everywhere. No word on how it applies to Garou in cultures that may be more &quot;past-oriented&quot; (for those who haven't dipped a toe into anthropology, there's an idea that some cultures tend towards past orientation, or centering the values and ways of one ancestors; present orientation, focusing mainly on living in the moment; and future orientation, focused mainly on what comes next and building towards the future; this does not apply to all people within those cultures but denotes cultural trends, but God knows I've seen some missteps where nursing textbooks have &quot;cultural considerations&quot; sections that talk about making adjustments for &quot;Indian time&quot;).<br /> <br /> I still think there's potential to build this out down the line, like how Forsaken eventually incorporated local folklores in a way to show how the Uratha had roots there and how their creation tale didn't necessarily override human folklore so much as syncretize with it. But the corebook shows that, if you try to strip out all the cultural elements you think you're getting wrong, you accidentally default back to the idea of a &quot;default&quot; culture which, in the West, is gonna be pretty damn Western.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28234,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28234-justincognito","user":"JustinCognito","date":". 12-15-2023, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28234-justincognito","name":"JustinCognito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T23:04:34-08:00","id":1526900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JustinCognito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526885#post1526885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the corebook shows that, if you try to strip out all the cultural elements you think you're getting wrong, you accidentally default back to the idea of a &quot;default&quot; culture which, in the West, is gonna be pretty damn Western.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it is even worse since in trying to 'correct' the goofs of Legacy, W5's Western lens is firmly in the USia culturally afloat camp. The mentality that any sort of animism/genuine nature worship is fake. Which then erases not only Shinto and Ainu faiths from Japan, but ALSO plenty of Western ways animism appears.<br /> <br /> So in order to avoid angering Indigenous people (and still doing so by not understanding the assignment), they happily made the garou as rootless and capitalistic as the 'bad' humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T00:20:55-08:00","id":1526905,"title":"","content":"I think part of the issue of Werewolf 5 is that it is desperately trying to make the game as non-poiltical and generic as possible due to fears of racism as well as fascism and indigineous rights. However, the problem is that W:TA had VERY STRONG opinions on these topics. It was also opinions that were punk and very progressive for their time even if they were tone deaf.<br /> <br /> Native rights was baked into the background of W:TA.<br /> <br /> The Garou wronged the Native Americans and stole their land.<br /> <br /> The Garou committed genocide in the past and called it victory.<br /> <br /> The Garou did a number on the aborigines (who admittedly have a good argument that maybe they should still be around since, well, they're still around).<br /> <br /> The game is acting like it didn't take a stance of &quot;reparations for wronged peoples and colonialism&quot; which was....a big stance it took.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T00:54:20-08:00","id":1526908,"title":"","content":"As a note on the transphobia: agree to disagree, but I personally see it as a potential story hook just about justified by the Garou's cultural belief, with a side note of some Tribes and Septs 'nobody gives a fuck if you're still doing the kid producing thing' and some Septs just not giving a flying fuck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526883#post1526883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wanted PCs are suburban or urban youths who have little ties to anything outside cities and who are disconnected from their cultures. This could be a great starting point, but the book treats this disconnect as a GOOD thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know of two games that came out this year that are set up to feature city bound characters disconnected from their culture who awaken to supernatural powers. One uses this to explore ideas of identity, the crushing weight of society, bonds of friendship, and all around a lot of great themes with advice to tailor it to multiple styles of game, and the other features werewolves.<br /> <br /> I don't know what it says that the release I was excited for disgusts me while the one I literally stumbled across in my FLGS inspires me. Probably just that I want to play a transbien magical girl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T01:11:17-08:00","id":1526909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526908#post1526908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note on the transphobia: agree to disagree, but I personally see it as a potential story hook just about justified by the Garou's cultural belief, with a side note of some Tribes and Septs 'nobody gives a fuck if you're still doing the kid producing thing' and some Septs just not giving a flying fuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think there are situations where it makes sense and can create a good story. For example, I am of the mind that some Furies would be TERFs due to the nature of the tribe. But in general, it is good to think if the intolerance would have a place in such a non-christian culture.<br /> <br /> To the 'nobody gives a fuck as long as you produce kids' part, from what I understand of mammal sexuality, most are bisexual and mating season is a different beast from having sex for pleasure. So there can still be drama if a garou doesn't want to have kids at all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T01:35:11-08:00","id":1526910,"title":"","content":"I tend to run furies are genrally terfy rather than universally. I also tend to varyhow terf it is is from<br /> &quot;I don't feel comfortable having you in the tribe but i dont object to you being in another tribe.&quot; Over to &quot;I'm willing to neglect women's rights to undermine you.&quot; not to mention &quot;I'm secretly a traitor and I'm using it to stir the pot.&quot;<br /> <br /> Roughly speaking its the 50 year old mom-posie Parker bar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-16-2023, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T02:08:40-08:00","id":1526911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526909#post1526909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do think there are situations where it makes sense and can create a good story. For example, I am of the mind that some Furies would be TERFs due to the nature of the tribe. But in general, it is good to think if the intolerance would have a place in such a non-christian culture.<br /> <br /> To the 'nobody gives a fuck as long as you produce kids' part, from what I understand of mammal sexuality, most are bisexual and mating season is a different beast from having sex for pleasure. So there can still be drama if a garou doesn't want to have kids at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me of a friend of mine who made Black Fury porn about their ways of reproducing with their kinfolk without men. She was a very unique gal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T03:05:28-08:00","id":1526914,"title":"","content":"While I'm not too eager to relitigate the whole Black Fury TERFs thing... there's a very simple solution: The Elders of the Tribe are the TERFs, while the younger generations are rejecting that stance. It models the current divisions in real world feminist politics, and it keeps to WtA's themes of traditional Elders vs.open-to-new-ways youngsters. It works for legacy WtA where the Black Furies have undergone many ideological shifts over time, and it works for W5's more blunt old vs. new dynamics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T05:13:44-08:00","id":1526919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526914#post1526914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm not too eager to relitigate the whole Black Fury TERFs thing... there's a very simple solution: The Elders of the Tribe are the TERFs, while the younger generations are rejecting that stance. It models the current divisions in real world feminist politics, and it keeps to WtA's themes of traditional Elders vs.open-to-new-ways youngsters. It works for legacy WtA where the Black Furies have undergone many ideological shifts over time, and it works for W5's more blunt old vs. new dynamics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, while some less human-ish elders might be accepting, I do see it with that dynamic. It is by NO means universal, but I feel it is part of the tribe's flaws, they represent both the bad and the good in womanhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T14:22:46-08:00","id":1526943,"title":"","content":"Whenever werewolves are supposed to share mortal prejudices, I just simply don't have them do it.<br /> <br /> Transwomen are a concept that existed well before modern era and the Black Furies might as well accept them as spiritually women given they're a bunch of shapechangers.<br /> <br /> They don't have to be like the villain of that SANDMAN arc.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have enough FAKE supernatural prejudices that you don't have to touch the real ones. Sort of like why the Get being Nazis just platforms them and is a worse decision than ignoring the past of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T14:50:08-08:00","id":1526945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526911#post1526911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That reminds me of a friend of mine who made Black Fury porn about their ways of reproducing with their kinfolk without men. She was a very unique gal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Step 1: Follow Whiptail Lizard as your pack patron.<br /> <br /> Step 2: Spend 3 permanent Gnosis and you're done!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T17:41:46-08:00","id":1526954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition?p=1526914#post1526914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm not too eager to relitigate the whole Black Fury TERFs thing... there's a very simple solution: The Elders of the Tribe are the TERFs, while the younger generations are rejecting that stance. It models the current divisions in real world feminist politics, and it keeps to WtA's themes of traditional Elders vs.open-to-new-ways youngsters. It works for legacy WtA where the Black Furies have undergone many ideological shifts over time, and it works for W5's more blunt old vs. new dynamics.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm recalling correctly I believe its only ever the Elders in The Temple of Artemis that are explicitly called out as having TERFy views. I honestly can't see any real reason why any of the others would be especially not folks like Freebooters, Moon Daughters and Bacchantes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T18:35:20-08:00","id":1526957,"title":"","content":"Reconciling the Changing Ways 20th Paradox inserts with the Camps is a pain. Like I said, I'm not really interested in going over all that again. There's an official book that makes the Furies far more TERFy than most people would have otherwise assumed. Making it a generational issue is the easiest way to handle that disconnect if you're not just going to ignore it completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T11:11:38-08:00","id":1527435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526737-things-to-like-w5-for-or-why-so-many-people-hate-new-edition#post1526737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, after reading of W5 corebook, I can say... surprisengly, I like it. Didn't try the system, but lore is huge improvement for Garou. New edition in fact, retcon the bigger part of their crimes.<br /> Namely:<br /> 1) No more kinfolk, hense no more eugenic, sex slavery or bestiality in case of Lupus.<br /> 2) Impergium is something that happened so long ago that Garou themselves barely know what did actully happenthan. The 'Delirium-as-collective-human-mental-trauma' is just a theory.<br /> 3) War of Rage? Wtf is this? Considering, that other Fera are pretty much aliens who Garou barely know anything about.<br /> 4) No more Crinos-borned and descrimination toward them<br /> 5) Since Garou have no history anymore, just an oral tradition, there isn't invasion in Americas, War of Tears, Swords of Heimdal and other 'great deeds' Garou were so famous for. Well, at least for now. Not guilty until proven guilty, etc.<br /> 6) Finally, Vampires are not 'Wyrmlings' by default. Like, leeches are still cruel, lying and sneaky bastards... but that stereotype about vampires gonna support like almost any denizen of WoD. First and foremost, vampires themselves.<br /> <br /> TL/DR, authors retconed most of controversies that taunted WtA in past editions. I can't find any objective reason for haters to bush Garou. Now they are... eccentialy, they are pretty close to status of the &quot;good guys&quot;.<br /> what's wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>In short, Imo, because these were good hooks for stories and details that made the WOD richer, and more inconvenient for those who live in it, which is a special touch in the tone of the story, like &quot;people are bad and the world (genetics) in itself doesn't help you&quot;, and I've seen the argument: The world itself can be that way and we can't do anything about it, but a fictional world can be changed by the will of the creator, so there's no excuse for not making it morally &quot;perfect&quot;, there is nothing wrong with making a work that way, but I disagree. As for dealing with certain issues, it's a good idea to talk in session zero to avoid them and if it's possible to reach a consensus, you can say that you can't address it because for idiots, and you can change &quot;idiots&quot; for another word in that case, They will mess up, to be honest, idiots will mess up anyway, I speak from experience.<br /> <br /> That said, for me, none of these points would be a problem if when it was taken away they gave me something in return, but that wasn't the case, they took away Metis and Lupus... you know, even if it was as NPC or possible enemies, could put on a Crinos without any anomalies and this could be fine for me, but no, they removed an element; they removed the kinfolk, if it was a problem they could say that they were not genetically related (not necessarily), that they are just a people who know and interact with them in a given way and are the most likely partners for that reason, but no, they removed another element; Granted there are problematic parts in the Garou story (some would say that the story as a whole is problematic, but that's another story), but instead of just removing the problematic part, they decided to remove everything and claim amnesia, they removed yet another element; Umbra, I'm not even going to comment, I admit that I'm not that interested myself, but in something that is already becoming anemic in this point that would be something; Conclusion, the W5 isn't even that different, it just seems the same but weaker, drier, pessimistic, and with less to say. Could it be that they intend to expand W5 with more material that could be interesting and provide some answers? It's even possible, but until then I maintain my position.<br /> <br /> An extra that isn't even W5's fault, but I'll count it as a demerit too, every now and then I come across someone saying that W5 corrected and improved what previous editions did and the legacy was just to please... you should already imagine what comes next, it's worse than the V5 situation in some ways.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}